"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Mammoth end 6-game slide with 4-1 win over Avalanche","description":"— Vincent Trocheck scored a goal and assisted another to help the Utah Mammoth beat the Colorado Avalanche 4-1 on Wednesday night and snap a six-game losing streak.","story":"SALT LAKE CITY -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2563036/vincent-trocheck\">Vincent Trocheck</a> scored a goal and assisted another to help the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/utah/utah-mammoth\">Utah Mammoth</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/col/colorado-avalanche\">Colorado Avalanche</a> 4-1 on Wednesday night and snap a six-game losing streak.\n\n\r\n              Liam O’Brien, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149158/dmitri-simashev\">Dmitri Simashev</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3904191/kevin-stenlund\">Kevin Stenlund</a> scored goals for the Mammoth. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874732/sebastian-cossa\">Sebastian Cossa</a> made 30 stops.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3904177/mackenzie-blackwood\">Mackenzie Blackwood</a> tallied 25 saves for Colorado. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5835/jaden-schwartz\">Jaden Schwartz</a> scored the lone goal for the Avalanche.\n\n\r\n              O’Brien put Utah on the board at 5:22 of the second, blasting a one-timer from the faceoff circle for his first goal of the season.\n\n\r\n              Trocheck made it a two-goal lead with a power-play goal with 2:07 left in the second. He slid out to the circle and slapped the puck home off a crisp feed from Keller.\n\n\r\n              Utah went up 3-0 only 62 seconds into the third after Simashev snapped in the puck from the circle for a short-handed goal.\n\n\r\n              Colorado started both the second and third periods with power-play chances but were unable to capitalize.\n\n\r\n              Schwartz’s unassisted goal with 4:59 left helped the Avalanche avoid a shutout.\n\n\r\n              Stenlund capped the scoring on an empty netter with 2:08 remaining.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Avalanche: Host Anaheim on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              Mammoth: Host Anaheim on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://na01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Fhub%2Fnhl&data=05%7C02%7C%7C7df55516b4824ea300ae08df134b201b%7C84df9e7fe9f640afb435aaaaaaaaaaaa%7C1%7C0%7C639250885543797966%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=G2ZE7%2B%2BqQtkkt%2BdC3sL%2F%2BQOrQQ3SoPGszmeleHbeX%2BE%3D&reserved=0\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-19T06:19:34Z"}}